    <item>
      <title>Has Mohamed Salah broken FPL?  | GW11 Captaincy | FPL 2021/22</title>
      <link>http://www.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk</link>
      <description>Last time out Salah boasted an effective ownership of just under 200% among engaged FPL managers. 
Can his dominance of the captaincy continue against West Ham in Gameweek 11? And has the Liverpool winger essentially broken the game, leaving us with no choice but to captain him every Gameweek and leave only 10 places in our team to toy with? 
Joe and Tom discuss Salah's influence on the captaincy and whether FPL managers dare to look elsewhere for the armband.
 ━━━━━━━━━━━━━ 
