    <item>
      <title>FPL Gameweek 33 Scoutcast | Fantasy Premier League Tips 2020/21</title>
      <link>http://www.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk</link>
      <description>Joe and Seb are joined by Conor, aka FPLPrince from the FPL Fan Show, to look at the key issues facing Fantasy Premier League managers ahead of Gameweek 33.
 It has been a big week for Spurs, including the sacking of boss Jose Mourinho and Ryan Mason taking over first team coaching.
 Meanwhile, their top scorer Harry Kane (£11.8m) is injured, ahead of the North London side’s League Cup final with Manchester City. This Wembley encounter also means both finalists blank in Gameweek 33, along with their opponents Southampton and Fulham.
 For FPL managers this presents a raft of challenges ahead of Gameweek 33. Do they keep hold of Kane, even though his return date from injury is unknown? Is Heung-Min Son (£9.5m) surplus to requirements, or will he flourish under Mason’s temporary charge? And could Gareth Bale (£9.2m) and even Dele Alli (£7.4m) become FPL assets once again?
 Joe, Seb and Conor try to make sense of how Spurs fit in with their plans, especially given the club’s favourable fixtures from Gameweek 34.
 To compound matters there are further blank Gameweeks and doubles on the horizon. The Scoutcast trio explain their tentative plans for combating these further complications.
 Meanwhile, attacking defenders are on the agenda. Their potential to offer returns at both ends of the pitch could provide the boost FPL managers need to steal a march on their mini-league rivals.
 In addition, the Scoutcast crew also look back on their Gameweek 32 highs and lows as well as reveal their upcoming transfer and captaincy plans.
 Next four fixtures are frisked and Conor takes his turn to pick a differential.
 ━━━━━━━━━━━━━ 🏆 Want to improve your FPL Rank?
 Become a Fantasy Football Scout Member - https://bit.ly/2E54l2F ━━━━━━━━━━━━━ 📹 Subscribe:
