        <![CDATA[<p>Joe and Seb are joined by Conor, aka FPLPrince from the FPL Fan Show, to look at the key issues facing Fantasy Premier League managers ahead of Gameweek 33.</p> <p>It has been a big week for Spurs, including the sacking of boss Jose Mourinho and Ryan Mason taking over first team coaching.</p> <p>Meanwhile, their top scorer Harry Kane (£11.8m) is injured, ahead of the North London side’s League Cup final with Manchester City. This Wembley encounter also means both finalists blank in Gameweek 33, along with their opponents Southampton and Fulham.</p> <p>For FPL managers this presents a raft of challenges ahead of Gameweek 33. Do they keep hold of Kane, even though his return date from injury is unknown? Is Heung-Min Son (£9.5m) surplus to requirements, or will he flourish under Mason’s temporary charge? And could Gareth Bale (£9.2m) and even Dele Alli (£7.4m) become FPL assets once again?</p> <p>Joe, Seb and Conor try to make sense of how Spurs fit in with their plans, especially given the club’s favourable fixtures from Gameweek 34.</p> <p>To compound matters there are further blank Gameweeks and doubles on the horizon. The Scoutcast trio explain their tentative plans for combating these further complications.</p> <p>Meanwhile, attacking defenders are on the agenda. Their potential to offer returns at both ends of the pitch could provide the boost FPL managers need to steal a march on their mini-league rivals.</p> <p>In addition, the Scoutcast crew also look back on their Gameweek 32 highs and lows as well as reveal their upcoming transfer and captaincy plans.</p> <p>Next four fixtures are frisked and Conor takes his turn to pick a differential.</p> <p>━━━━━━━━━━━━━ 🏆 Want to improve your FPL Rank?</p> <p>Become a Fantasy Football Scout Member - https://bit.ly/2E54l2F ━━━━━━━━━━━━━ 📹 Subscribe:</p> <p>Main channel - https://bit.ly/392PzEY Second channel - https://bit.ly/3j5ze7j ━━━━━━━━━━━━━ Follow Fantasy Football Scout:</p> <p>💸 Twitter: https:/