    <item>
      <title>FPL Gameweek 32 Scoutcast | Fantasy Premier League Tips 2020/21</title>
      <link>http://www.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk</link>
      <description>Joe and Seb are joined by Tom Stephenson, who is second in the Fantasy Football Scout Live Hall of Fame, to look at the key issues facing Fantasy Premier League managers ahead of Gameweek 32.
 Jesse Lingard (£6.5m)’s brace at the weekend was just the latest in his eight-goals scoring spree, since joining West Ham on loan earlier this year.
 Meanwhile, Burnley forward Matej Vydra (£4.8m) now has three goals in his last five matches, after scoring against Newcastle in Gameweek 31, and Chelsea’s Mason Mount (£7.2m) added to his 12 goals and assists for the campaign during his Saturday visit to Crystal Palace.
 All are in fine form but are among players who are being often too readily dismissed by many FPL managers.
 This latest episode pays tribute to these unfashionable players in the game. Can FPL managers benefit by looking beyond their often lowly price tags or past failures?
 To help Seb and Tom take a trip down the catwalk of outmoded players, is Tom, who has never ended a season outside the top 36k in his long career and is currently in pole position for another strong finish.
 Seb takes a look at how FPL managers can benefit from taking time to look logically at players and address biases, while Tom details some of the players he may have unfairly overlooked this season. Joe joins in the chat to showcase his table of some of the latest behind the times stars, who are posting strong underlying statistics.
 Elsewhere, Tottenham enjoy a double Gameweek 32. Is Harry Kane worth a Triple Captain chip and is there a case for not maximising Spurs coverage this time around?
 Tom, Seb and Joe tackle your other burning questions on the North London side, as well as  Leicester’s strong fixtures and a changing of the guard among mid-price midfielders.
 The Scoutcast crew also look back on their Gameweek 31 highs and lows as well, as those of the community in ‘rough with the smooth’.
 Transfer and captaincy plans are revealed, next four fixtures are frisked and Tom takes his turn to pick a differential. In keeping with the show an unfashionable player, with potential for points at both ends of the pitch, is firmly in his sights.
 ━━━━━━━━━━━━━ 🏆 Want to improve your FPL Rank?
 Become a Fantasy Football Scout Member - https://bit.ly/2E54l2F ━━━━━━━━━━━━━ 📹 Subscribe:
