    <item>
      <title>FPL Gameweek 30 Scoutcast | Fantasy Premier League Tips 2020/21</title>
      <link>http://www.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk</link>
      <description>Joe, Ted from Ted Talks FPL, and Fantasy Football Scout owner Chris look at the key issues facing Fantasy Premier League managers ahead of Gameweek 30.
 On Tuesday afternoon, just minutes before Joe was about to send his Scoutcast production notes over to Ted and Chris, the Premier League announced the next double gameweek of the season.
 After a quick rewrite, the crew were as prepared as they could be for Tuesday night’s live show to discuss the news that Tottenham will face both Everton and Southampton in Gameweek 32.
 For Joe and Chris this means tweaking their wildcard plans for Gameweek 31, with Spurs assets understandably taking centre stage. Will Joe use the North London side’s extra fixture to deploy his bench boost as well? These and many more issues are considered during the episode.
 Meanwhile, a chipless Ted is left wondering what to do with, possibly out of favour, Spurs star Gareth Bale (£9.7m), who is currently in his side.
 In addition to this look ahead to the coming week’s fixture mayhem, the Scoutcast trio chat about Gameweek 30’s one week punts. Could this week’s top defensive differential pick help propel FPL managers up their mini-leagues?
 Elsewhere, Ted drops his latest graphs, detailing the players who are most likely to score and the teams which are prone to concede.
 The events of Blank Gameweek 29 are mulled over and, crucially, Joe, Ted and Chris reveal their captaincy and transfer plans for the full set of fixtures that await over the Easter weekend.
 ━━━━━━━━━━━━━ 🏆 Want to improve your FPL Rank?
