    <item>
      <title>FPL Gameweek 29 Scoutcast | Fantasy Premier League Tips 2020/21</title>
      <link>http://www.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk</link>
      <description>Joe, Seb and Fantasy Football Scout editor David look at the key issues facing Fantasy Premier League managers ahead of Gameweek 29.
 With just four fixtures, the weekend’s schedule looks particularly uninspiring.
 Tottenham’s Harry Kane (£11.5m) looks the standout captaincy pick, ahead of the North London side’s clash with Aston Villa. In addition, there could be plenty of low owned gems and bargain point scorers to help propel FPL managers up the rankings.
 Our trio sift through each fixture to find the likeliest sources of goals, assists and clean sheets.
 Attacking defenders are also looked at in detail, as Joe, Seb and David try to find players who can return at both ends of the pitch.
 Seb takes his turn to pick a differential, Joe pitches a new TV show involving West Ham’s on loan star Jesse Lingard (£6.1m) and David reveals more about Fulham than the Scoutcast bargained for.
 There’s next four fixtures to frisk too. This will help FPL managers look beyond Blank Gameweek 29 to reveal the twists and turns of the schedule over the next month.
 Rough with the Smooth returns and the crew also look at their Gameweek 28 scores so far.
 ━━━━━━━━━━━━━ 🏆 Want to improve your FPL Rank?
