    <item>
      <title>FPL GW26 SCOUTCAST | Double Gameweek 26 Guide | Fantasy Premier League Tips 2020/21</title>
      <link>http://www.fantasyfootballscout.co.uk</link>
      <description>Joe is joined by David and Karam to look at the key issues facing Fantasy Premier League managers ahead of double Gameweek 26.
 With 14 teams playing twice and six more having a single fixture, Gameweek 26 looks to be the biggest double Gameweek in FPL history.
 There’s a lot for the Scoutcast crew to take in, with chips and captaincy among some of the issues to consider.
 They also have to plan for future double and blank Gameweeks and still ensure they target the right players for the weekend.
 Luckily Karam is on hand to help frame the discussion as he unleashes his wildcard on the Gameweek.
 Are Everton and Tottenham assets the best to target for the captaincy this time around, especially with such favourable fixtures? Or are more reliable premium assets such as Manchester United talisman Bruno Fernandes (£11.6m) a shrewder pick? And what of the cast of low owned gems to consider, with Leicester’s Harvey Barnes already being picked up by thousands of FPL managers ahead of the weekend.
 Our trio take time to recap on their Gameweek 25 scores too, as well as frisk the fixtures over the next month and firm up their transfer and captaincy plans.
 For Karam especially he is hoping he can set up a team for a number of weeks, not just the impending set of double fixtures. This is especially important as he prepares for his wedding next month. Many congratulations from all at the Scoutcast ahead of  his special day.
